{The policy inherits Parents 1 and 3’s dispersion-driven H0 emphasis, Parent 0’s progress-dependent shift toward H1, and Parent 4’s readiness-dispersion adjustment. Both H1-directed adjustments weaken when remaining-work dispersion is high, preserving H0’s explicit long-work reward against H1’s preference for smaller finish-plus-tail estimates; readiness dispersion is treated only as an aggregate signal, not a bottleneck identifier. This bounded blend is a hypothesis for external complete-schedule evaluation, not a claim of state-level superiority.}
